# The rule here: anything that cannot be regenerated gets tracked.
# Source data, notes, decisions and sweep outputs are all irreplaceable —
# Yahoo Finance revises its series, and the sweeps cost days of CPU.
# Only caches, environments and build artefacts are excluded.
# Whole repo is ~76MB tracked, which is well inside GitHub's limits.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environments and editors
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Training scratch — regenerable, or vendor-specific
runs/
wandb/
tb_logs/
*.log
slurm-logs/
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err

# Model checkpoints — large, and reproducible from the configs + seeds
*.pt
*.pkl
*.zip

# LaTeX build output
**/build/
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.out
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.run.xml

# --- Deliberately TRACKED, listed here so the reason is on record ---
# data/raw/*.csv        source VIX + S&P, 1.9MB. Yahoo re-downloads are not
#                       byte-identical, so this is the only provenance record.
# results/              windows.csv, steps.csv, summary.json, training curves.
#                       60MB, and the only alternative to 2.7 days of retraining.
# *.md                  decisions log, research log, handoff, to-do, journey.
#                       The project's reasoning lives here and nowhere else.
# claude-read/          project context and standing instructions.
# takeoff/, defence/    deck, speaker notes, defence guide.
# plots/                generated, but cheap to keep and useful in history.
